 ## Overview
-Feature Fields generalize the Neural Radiance Field (NeRF) formulation to predict arbitrary per-point feature signals $\mathbf{f}$ in addition to color $\mathbf{c}$ and density $\sigma$ [S1, unofficial]. This extension enables the lifting of 2D observations—such as semantic labels, object codes, or foundation model embeddings—into a consistent 3D representation, solving the limitation of NeRF as a purely photometric model [S1, S2, unofficial]. Unlike sibling methods that modify the input space (e.g., [MS-NeRF](11707-multi-space-neural-radiance-field-ms-nerf.md)) or use separate networks for specific tasks (e.g., [NRFF](12072-nrff.md)), this family integrates these signals directly into the volume rendering pipeline, allowing 2D supervision to lift into a consistent 3D representation [S1, unofficial][S3].
