 ### Object Field Representation
-**Definition:** A function $f(\mathbf{p})$ that maps a 3D point $\mathbf{p}$ to an object code vector $\mathbf{o}$, representing object ownership independent of viewing angles [S2, unofficial].
-**Parameters:** $H$ is the predefined maximum number of solid objects the network predicts; a relatively large value is chosen in practice [S2, unofficial]. The function $f$ is parameterized by a series of MLPs [S2, unofficial].
-**Pitfall:** The variable number of objects and large non-occupied volumes are solved by fixing the dimension to $H+1$, reserving the last dimension for empty space to handle occlusion/collision [S2, unofficial].
